{% comment %}
  Preset Documentation
  
  This snippet provides documentation and examples for using the theme's
  preset system in sections. It explains all available presets (color schemes,
  typography, spacing, layouts) and shows how to implement them in section
  schemas and liquid templates. Include this as a comment in your section
  files for reference when building new sections.
  
  This snippet provides documentation for using presets in sections.
  Include this as a comment in your section files for reference.

  
  Available Presets:
  
  Color Schemes:
  - light: Light color scheme with white background
  - dark: Dark color scheme with dark background
  - vibrant: Vibrant colors with bright accents
  - minimal: Minimal color scheme with neutral tones
  - warm: Warm color scheme with earth tones
  
  Typography Presets:
  - modern: Modern typography with bold headings
  - classic: Classic typography with balanced weights
  - bold: Bold typography with heavy weights
  - elegant: Elegant typography with refined spacing
  
  Spacing Presets:
  - compact: Tight spacing for dense layouts
  - standard: Standard spacing for balanced layouts
  - spacious: Generous spacing for open layouts
  
  Layout Variations:
  - grid: Grid layout for cards/products
  - list: List layout for vertical content
  - masonry: Masonry layout for varied heights
  - centered: Centered layout for hero sections
  
  Usage Example:
  
  In section schema, add:
  
  {
    "type": "select",
    "id": "color_scheme_override",
    "label": "Color Scheme Override",
    "default": "",
    "options": [
      { "value": "", "label": "Use theme default" },
      { "value": "light", "label": "Light" },
      { "value": "dark", "label": "Dark" },
      { "value": "vibrant", "label": "Vibrant" },
      { "value": "minimal", "label": "Minimal" },
      { "value": "warm", "label": "Warm" }
    ]
  }
  
  In section liquid, use:
  
  {% liquid
    assign color_scheme = section.settings.color_scheme_override | default: ''
    assign section_class = 'my-section'
    if color_scheme != blank
      assign section_class = section_class | append: ' scheme-' | append: color_scheme
    endif
  %}
  
  <div class="{{ section_class }}">
    <!-- Section content -->
  </div>
{% endcomment %}

